Upon receiving the **DEREGISTRATION ACCEPT** message, the UE shall delete any stored:

- 5G-GUTI;
- last visited registered TAI;
- TAI list;
- allowed NSSAI;
- configured NSSAI;
- mapping of allowed NSSAI; and
- rejected NSSAI, if any.

The UE shall delete the stored 5GMM context, i.e.:

- the **5G-GUTI**;
- the **TAI list**;
- the **allowed NSSAI** and any **mapping of allowed NSSAI**;
- the **configured NSSAI** and any **mapping of configured NSSAI**;
- the **rejected NSSAI** (if present);
- the **list of equivalent PLMNs**; and
- the **UE security context** (including the ngKSI).

This applies for the relevant access type when the DEREGISTRATION REQUEST carries the specified abnormal 5GMM causes and indicates **“re-registration not required.”**

When the UE requests both MICO mode with active time and eDRX, the network can decide to:

- accept MICO mode with active time and eDRX;
- accept MICO mode with active time and reject eDRX;
- reject MICO mode with active time and accept eDRX; or
- reject both MICO mode with active time and eDRX.
